WEBVTT

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.340
You came to get me?

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.430
Pain

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.610
Tora-san.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.310
I guess that was just a dream.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:46.710
I'm off then.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.490
Good morning.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.550
Thank you for last night.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.270
Great Passage

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:20.610
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:26.750
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.390
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:39.830
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.340
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:52.650
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:59.620
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:06.130
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:12.670
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:19.140
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.220
Love

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.760
Souunsou

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.630
Thank you for everything you do for my
grandmother.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.400
I'm her granddaughter, Kaguya Hayashi.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.800
She's letting me stay here for a while.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.270
I was actually supposed to be
coming a little later,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.770
but my work asked me to start earlier.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.410
Work?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.680
I'm training to be a Japanese chef.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.580
Japanese... chef?

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.850
It's a place in Yushima called Ume no Mi.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.820
I see.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:15.230
I'm sorry, I must be in your way.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:18.970
Have a good day.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.500
Okay.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.540
Did Micchan leave?

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.680
I was going to talk to him about you.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.650
We've already introduced ourselves.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.960
But maybe I was the only one
really talking.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.900
I couldn't say a word at all.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.270
Not a single... word.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.510
No way I could do that!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:08.510
Why can't I ever say...

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.020
what I want to?

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.730
Sanyodou

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.300
What?

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.270
What's wrong with him?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.370
Morning. What's up?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.440
It's nothing.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.050
Is that the guy you were talking about?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.750
Good morning!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.320
Good morning.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:50.720
Good morning.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.930
What was that earlier with him?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.700
Oh, well.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.870
All right, let's get this started.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.910
- Just ask if you've got questions.
- Okay.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.910
Thank you very much

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.780
Daijirin

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.460
Machine Language.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.330
Kojien

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:56.890
Mechanical engineering.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.970
I've gotta do this for ten more years?!

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.410
It might be even longer for you, Nishioka.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.610
I'll change jobs before then.

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:58.650
You know,

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.890
I was spending time with my nephew,
and he asked for a cell phone.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.420
He's still in elementary school.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.190
Kids are so precocious these days.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.100
Precocious?

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.070
Precocious.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.770
Omase is used regardless of gender,
but oshama is only used with girls.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.210
They both mean precocious.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.140
So, what is the difference?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.580
Is that what you took from my story?

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:33.450
Why do I have to help too?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.860
An uninhibited girl.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.790
Tomboy. Shrew.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.830
Hoyden?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:46.830
All right, fine.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.740
I'll help you out.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.780
Thank you very much.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.660
I guess there really are people

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.530
who were born to make dictionaries.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:26.240
Araki-san and Matsumoto-sensei should
be arriving soon.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.110
Today's our monthly meeting.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.680
I will make the preparations.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.180
Majime-san, please continue selecting the
entry words.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:40.290
- Okay.
- You too, Nishioka.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.050
All right.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.090
I will go get the snacks.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.070
Now what?

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.640
Something up with this?

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.740
Why...?

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.240
This morning... I couldn't...

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.580
I couldn't even say anything...

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.050
distance

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.260
Majime-chan!
Are you in love or something?

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.890
Love?

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.830
Love

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.930
Love.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.060
Bingo, huh?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.870
So, what's she like?
She cute?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.900
I'd be happy to give you some advice.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.610
Under the same roof?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.080
That's so freaking hot!

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:44.020
Listen up. You have to control yourself,
okay?

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.950
So how old is she?

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.290
I don't know yet.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.790
She is apparently a Japanese chef.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:52.760
So she seems to be working.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:56.160
Come on. You have to ask for basic
information from the get go...

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.960
...if you want things to work out.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.900
What am I supposed to do about it?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.740
I've never... really been that forward with...
any girl before...

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.170
Wait, you're not saying...

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.280
Are you a virgin?

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.900
monthly meeting

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.370
So how're you finding the work, Majime?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.340
Oh, yes. It's very fun.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.310
Is that right?

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.610
This is what he's done so far.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.680
Wow, this much already?

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.850
How do you not get bored with it?

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:33.850
It's proof of his passion for words.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:35.620
I'd better pick up the pace too.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.750
Come on.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:40.390
You know, I've worked hard
all this time too,

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:43.160
and you've never said
anything like that to me.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.860
I'll acknowledge that you discovered
Shippouen.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.300
Yes. And you're the one who introduced
me to Shaoxing wine.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:53.440
Out of everything I've done,
that's all I get credit for?

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.310
The restaurant for last year's New Year's
party was nice.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.770
Yeah, that place was delicious!

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.640
Not you too, Sasaki-san.

00:11:00.780 --> 00:11:04.880
What do you all think I am?

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:15.190
Let us strive to create definitions
with modern sensibilities.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.860
We will include many proverbs,
technical terms,

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.430
and proper nouns into Daitokai.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:23.430
We want a dictionary that
can be used as an encyclopedia.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.530
Regarding that, Araki...

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:28.900
Lately, I've been hearing about this IT
field.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:32.840
It stands for information technology.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:36.980
Unfortunately,
I understand nothing about it,

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.820
but it is something young people
are inundated with.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:48.620
So, what do you think about including as
many IT related words into Daitokai?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.890
I see. That is a good point.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.300
Do either you know much
about computers?

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.970
I can touch type. But that's about it.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.700
I'm not very good with machines...

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.640
I see. Well, that's fine.
Just keep it in mind.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.770
Okay.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.910
I will immediately make a list
of informatics experts.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.510
Thank you.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.880
There's something
I'd like you all to remember.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:15.480
A dictionary like Daitokai

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:20.920
will have so many more words
than it will have editors.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.830
In order to incorporate words
from a diverse field

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:27.830
we each must show interest
in a variety of things

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.600
and remember to do away with our biases.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:37.940
If you run into any concerns or have ideas,
please do not hesitate to share them.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.380
Oh, in that case.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.510
This guy's apparently a virgin.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:48.550
Does being a virgin somehow affect his
ability to compile a dictionary?

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.550
Actually, it does.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:53.920
Majime froze up when he saw a card.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.930
How can he get any work done
if he freezes every time

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.400
he comes across a card
that reminds him of the girl he likes.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.030
This is coming from you?

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.900
Is there a young lady you've fallen for?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:10.470
Sensei! There's no need to humor
Nishioka with his nonsense.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.010
No, Araki.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.410
Love and companionship
are a vital part of life.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:19.750
We must offer our everything
to the dictionary.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.020
Our time, our money.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:25.520
We only reserve the bare minimum
to live our lives,

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.890
and the rest must be devoted
to the dictionary.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.460
Family vacations, amusement parks...

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:35.630
I know the words, but I've never
experienced them myself.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:40.070
Determining if it's someone who would
understand such a commitment

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.770
is quite important.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:46.110
Sensei, don't you think
you're getting a little heavy.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:49.380
What is this person like?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.050
Apparently, she's a Japanese chef.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.720
Pretty unusual for a girl, isn't it?

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.620
Is it?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.990
What restaurant does she work at?

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.890
A place called Ume no Mi in Yushima.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.790
Is this the place?

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:06.930
Ume no Mi

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:09.670
Of course you'd be so on top of this.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:14.470
I was looking at it thinking that we could
go for Japanese sometime.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.640
What do you say?
Why don't we go there tonight?

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:20.910
That's a wonderful idea.
Is everybody free tonight?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.950
I'm free.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.780
I will be fine as long as I call home first.

00:14:25.910 --> 00:14:28.080
What about you, Majime-san?

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.890
Okay.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.820
- I mean, no.
- All right, I'll make the reservation!

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.160
He just does whatever he wants.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.430
I got the reservations!

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.100
Majime-chan!

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.700
Here's some advice.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.770
In order to truly understand a word

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:54.040
you'll need some real world experience
to have it really register, don't you think?

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.680
Let's take this romance to the next level!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.190
Well, now...

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.460
I'm speechless.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.730
What a very pretty girl.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.630
Majime, you dog.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.570
This is tofu misozuke.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.540
Please eat it with a spoon.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.080
I'm surprised that you came so soon.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.850
Majime told us about you.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.980
Your name is Kaguya-san, isn't it?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.880
That's a nice name.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.750
It just means
I was born under the full moon.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:42.690
What made you decide to become a
Japanese chef?

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.460
I love to cook.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.800
But it must be hard
with the early mornings.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:51.930
Yeah! And I hear it takes years
to be considered ready.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.470
But I love it.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:57.670
No matter how many years it takes,
I want to become a Japanese chef.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.510
That is similar to our work.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.620
We are making a dictionary.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:10.750
Completing a dictionary is also
an endeavor that takes years.

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:14.220
Really? You're making a dictionary?

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.120
That's nice.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.160
Well, please enjoy your meal.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:21.200
Sensei.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:27.940
She's a nice girl, Majime-san.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:32.840
She is trying to master something
like we are.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:37.050
Understanding that it takes time
in order to do so

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.250
makes her a very suitable partner.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:43.790
I'm sure she'll be someone
you could lean on.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:46.120
Thank you.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.190
You're not even going out yet.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.660
Oh, yes. Of course.

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:52.900
Well, good luck.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.860
I'm sure it'll work out.
You share a roof after all.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.600
Yes, I'll do my best.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:05.010
I want to complete what I'm doing as well,
no matter how many years it takes.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.050
Man, that Kaguya was cute.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.020
Seriously, don't blow it.

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:19.990
You barely talked to her.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:23.590
How can I be more like you?

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.090
What? Me?

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:28.600
You're able to talk to people so
comfortably at work and everywhere.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.330
That's nothing special.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:34.140
Being able to say what you think
is difficult.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:36.340
Are you making fun of me?

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:39.310
No! I really think it's amazing.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:42.840
You're able to create a good environment
for everyone.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:44.880
What? I just get chastised.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.280
Mostly by Araki-san.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.350
But you make everything fun for everyone.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:50.920
You think so?

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.160
You're really amazing.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.690
You're the amazing one.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.690
No, you are much more amazing.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:02.730
I can't elevate a conversation like you can.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.900
I don't know how to engage
Kaguya-san at all.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.140
I'm just...

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:15.780
Now, what?

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:18.880
That's right! To depend on each other!

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.620
This is what she meant!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.090
If I can't do something,
I should just depend on others!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.950
This is the way I can become closer!

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.690
Who taught you that?

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:29.990
How did you know
someone taught me that?

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.400
It's obvious.

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.240
What a weird guy.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:46.680
How did I get stuck
working with a guy like him?

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.780
But when he dragged me into
all that hard work today

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:58.150
looking up the meanings and differences
between words...

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.190
That was pretty fun.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.870
Hope.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:14.300
Sixteenth night of the month.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:16.910
Sixteen-day-old moon.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:21.110
He's a weird guy,

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.680
but maybe things will be more interesting.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.250
Nothing!

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.060
Dictionary Editorial Department

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:44.800
Oh, where's Nishioka?

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.070
He went to the bathroom.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.870
So he went to the main building.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:19:59.750
You're so stupid.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.050
Oh, so did you hear?

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:03.820
- What?
- Well, it's just a rumor.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.150
You know that plan
to make a new dictionary?

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:08.020
They're talking about canceling it.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:12.130
- I mean dictionaries are a real money pit.
- Yeah. It's not surprising.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:16.060
- We all have our problems.
- But you know...

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:18.400
What?

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.910
Love: To fancy someone.
"He fell in love and the chest hurt"

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:40.960
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:51.970
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:20:53.340 --> 00:21:03.810
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:10.520
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:16.360
So please stay the way you are

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:22.460
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:27.940
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:40.850
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.830
You're still new to dictionary work.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.260
Feel free to ask me anything.

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.170
Nishioka-san.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.330
Could you explain this--

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:02.570
How would I know
something complicated like that?

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.240
So true.
